  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Backend Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the backend architecture. My initial thought is to begin by outlining the necessary files. I\'ve started with `server/db.ts`, which will handle in-memory storage, file backups, and include pre-seeded realistic data from sources like RemoteOK, Greenhouse, and Lever.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Services**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out core services. `aiService.ts` will wrap the Gemini SDK, providing functions for resume parsing, job matching, cover letter generation, and more, including email classification and an agent step runner. Concurrently, `jobService.ts` will handle job adapters from various sources, incorporating deduplication and pre-filters. Finally, `applicationService.ts` focuses on dynamic application preparation, generating cover letters, and handling AI-answered questions.\n\n\n**Expanding Service Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into service implementation. I\'ve got `telegramService.ts` sending real Telegram messages if configured, matching templates outlined earlier and logging to the in-app feed. `emailService.ts` ingests emails, uses `classifyEmail`, links to applications, and updates status, dispatching Telegram notifications. I\'m also working on `agentLoop.ts`, a ReAct agent, and `schedulerService.ts` for automated routines. I will then move on to the express router handling endpoints in `api.ts`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 25
      nanos: 136664445
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
