    thinking: "**Exploring Job API Feeds**\n\nOkay, I\'m now exploring real-time job fetching using free public APIs, specifically focusing on `RemoteOK` to begin with. I\'m keen to incorporate this live data feed to make the application truly dynamic and up-to-date.\n\n\n**Expanding Job API Integration**\n\nI\'m now investigating additional API feeds to enhance job data sources. I\'m focusing on `Arbeitnow` for European and US tech jobs, and `Remotive` for worldwide remote tech jobs. I am also planning on building direct ingestion for URLs or raw text. My goal is to build a very dynamic and inclusive job ingestion process.\n\nI\'m also working on building the resume parser and importer functionality. It will handle PDF, DOCX, TXT, MD, and JSON files, or text pasted by the user. Gemini will populate the user\'s skills, experience, and preferences.\n\nI\'m also aiming to provide users with a resume download in Markdown or a printable format. Next up, I will work on integrating job ingestion directly into the `JobsView.tsx` component via a new \'Import Job by URL or Text\' button, and immediate compatibility evaluation.\n\n\n**Implementing Application Automation**\n\nI\'ve integrated one-click application autofill with clipboard assistants within the `ApplicationApprovalModal.tsx`. I\'ve added copy buttons for cover letters and answers, a button to launch external job postings, and instant export options as PDF or Markdown. I\'m now testing the Telegram bot integration to dispatch real messages for high-match jobs and application approvals. Finally, I\'m working on a real inbound classifier that parses recruiter emails and updates job stages.\n\n\n"
