  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining User Requirements**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on the user\'s explicit needs. They require a daily automated report at 10 AM via Telegram, summarizing at least five job applications. The process must also involve proper email notifications, and I understand I may need the user\'s Gmail for this function. I\'m focusing on parsing the input request for key requirements.\n\n\n**Testing System Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a basic test to verify that the system functions correctly. I am asking myself, do I need to deploy this, or can I just use it as it is? I\'m designing a function that runs at 10 AM, dispatching jobs over Telegram. The user can set time, number of apps, email. The code needs to run and notify, and also allow the user to test the 10:00 routine manually.\n\n\n**Refining Automation Process**\n\nI\'m now incorporating job sourcing from various platforms like RemoteOK, Arbeitnow, Remotive, Greenhouse, and Lever. Subsequently, I\'m integrating a Gemini model to assess candidate fit, selecting the top five matches (with scores of 80% or higher). The system generates complete application packages, including personalized cover letters and form fields, then submits these. Finally, it sends a comprehensive Telegram digest, formatted with Markdown, to provide the user with a convenient daily summary.\n\n\n**Implementing Email Delivery**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented the email dispatch functionality! A formatted morning digest, as an HTML/text email, is now being sent to the user\'s specified address. I also included SMTP configuration in the settings to allow for Gmail SMTP credentials or direct API delivery. Additionally, a single-click button to run the 10:00 AM test is now available across the agent console, dashboard, and settings tabs!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 46319685
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
