  planner_response {
    response: "The system has been set up with the **10:00 AM Daily Morning Routine**, **Gmail SMTP Email Dispatch**, and **Telegram Notification Pipeline**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How to Test the System Right Now\n\nYou can test the entire end-to-end pipeline in one click without waiting for tomorrow morning:\n\n1. Look at the **Top Banner on the Dashboard** or go to the **Settings** tab.\n2. Click the **`\342\232\241 Test 10:00 AM Routine (5 Applied)`** button.\n3. **What will happen automatically:**\n   - **Multi-Source Job Scan**: Searches live job boards (RemoteOK, Greenhouse, Lever, etc.).\n   - **AI Match Evaluation**: Gemini scores matches against your candidate profile.\n   - **5+ Applications Prepared & Applied**: Bespoke, truthful cover letters and application forms are generated and marked as submitted.\n   - **Telegram Notification**: Formats and sends a markdown summary with all applied jobs directly to your Telegram chat.\n   - **Email Digest**: Generates an HTML job application digest and dispatches it to your Gmail (`codepankaj84@gmail.com`).\n   - **Live In-App Logs**: You can view the live actions in the **Agent Console** and the email records in the **Email Monitor** tab.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Connect Your Gmail for Real Outbound Emails\n\nTo have the agent send real emails directly through your Gmail account:\n\n1. Go to your **Google Account** \342\206\222 **Security** \342\206\222 **2-Step Verification** \342\206\222 **App Passwords**.\n2. Create an App Password (name it e.g. `JobAgent`). Google will generate a 16-character password (e.g. `abcd efgh ijkl mnop`).\n3. Open the **Settings** tab in the app.\n4. In the **Email Dispatch & Gmail SMTP Settings** card:\n   - **Recipient Email**: `codepankaj84@gmail.com`\n   - **Gmail SMTP User**: `codepankaj84@gmail.com`\n   - **Gmail App Password**: Enter the 16-character App Password.\n5. Click **Save Email Settings**, then click **Send Test Email** to verify your SMTP connection immediately.\n\n*(Note: Even without SMTP credentials configured, the system logs and renders full email digests in the built-in **Email Monitor** tab).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Do You Need to Deploy It Anywhere?\n\nHere is the breakdown of how execution works:\n\n- **As it is right now (in AI Studio Preview):**\n  - The agent, scheduler, API server, and user interface run actively inside the container.\n  - The minute-checker is running every 45 seconds to detect `10:00 AM`.\n  - However, preview containers may go to sleep if inactive or if you close your browser tab for an extended period.\n\n- **For 24/7 autonomous daily execution (when your computer is off):**\n  - **Yes, deploying to a persistent cloud environment is recommended** so that the backend server stays alive 24/7 without needing your laptop open.\n  - **Recommended Deployment Options:**\n    1. **Deploy to Cloud Run / Render / Railway / Fly.io / VPS**:\n       - Run `npm run build` followed by `npm start`.\n       - Set environment variables (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, etc.).\n       - The built-in scheduler will run continuously and trigger every morning at 10:00 AM.\n    2. **External Cron Trigger**:\n       - You can also set up a free scheduled cron job (e.g., via GitHub Actions or cron-job.org) to ping your server\'s endpoint:\n         `POST /api/scheduler/morning-routine` every day at `10:00 AM`."
    thinking: "**Clarifying Testing Options**\n\nI\'m focusing now on clear instructions for testing. The primary thought revolves around enabling one-click testing of the 10:00 AM pipeline. This would involve a new button, likely labeled \"\342\232\241 Test 10:00 AM Routine Now\". This simplifies the validation process for the user, and is my current priority.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The system has been set up with the **10:00 AM Daily Morning Routine**, **Gmail SMTP Email Dispatch**, and **Telegram Notification Pipeline**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How to Test the System Right Now\n\nYou can test the entire end-to-end pipeline in one click without waiting for tomorrow morning:\n\n1. Look at the **Top Banner on the Dashboard** or go to the **Settings** tab.\n2. Click the **`\342\232\241 Test 10:00 AM Routine (5 Applied)`** button.\n3. **What will happen automatically:**\n   - **Multi-Source Job Scan**: Searches live job boards (RemoteOK, Greenhouse, Lever, etc.).\n   - **AI Match Evaluation**: Gemini scores matches against your candidate profile.\n   - **5+ Applications Prepared & Applied**: Bespoke, truthful cover letters and application forms are generated and marked as submitted.\n   - **Telegram Notification**: Formats and sends a markdown summary with all applied jobs directly to your Telegram chat.\n   - **Email Digest**: Generates an HTML job application digest and dispatches it to your Gmail (`codepankaj84@gmail.com`).\n   - **Live In-App Logs**: You can view the live actions in the **Agent Console** and the email records in the **Email Monitor** tab.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Connect Your Gmail for Real Outbound Emails\n\nTo have the agent send real emails directly through your Gmail account:\n\n1. Go to your **Google Account** \342\206\222 **Security** \342\206\222 **2-Step Verification** \342\206\222 **App Passwords**.\n2. Create an App Password (name it e.g. `JobAgent`). Google will generate a 16-character password (e.g. `abcd efgh ijkl mnop`).\n3. Open the **Settings** tab in the app.\n4. In the **Email Dispatch & Gmail SMTP Settings** card:\n   - **Recipient Email**: `codepankaj84@gmail.com`\n   - **Gmail SMTP User**: `codepankaj84@gmail.com`\n   - **Gmail App Password**: Enter the 16-character App Password.\n5. Click **Save Email Settings**, then click **Send Test Email** to verify your SMTP connection immediately.\n\n*(Note: Even without SMTP credentials configured, the system logs and renders full email digests in the built-in **Email Monitor** tab).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Do You Need to Deploy It Anywhere?\n\nHere is the breakdown of how execution works:\n\n- **As it is right now (in AI Studio Preview):**\n  - The agent, scheduler, API server, and user interface run actively inside the container.\n  - The minute-checker is running every 45 seconds to detect `10:00 AM`.\n  - However, preview containers may go to sleep if inactive or if you close your browser tab for an extended period.\n\n- **For 24/7 autonomous daily execution (when your computer is off):**\n  - **Yes, deploying to a persistent cloud environment is recommended** so that the backend server stays alive 24/7 without needing your laptop open.\n  - **Recommended Deployment Options:**\n    1. **Deploy to Cloud Run / Render / Railway / Fly.io / VPS**:\n       - Run `npm run build` followed by `npm start`.\n       - Set environment variables (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, etc.).\n       - The built-in scheduler will run continuously and trigger every morning at 10:00 AM.\n    2. **External Cron Trigger**:\n       - You can also set up a free scheduled cron job (e.g., via GitHub Actions or cron-job.org) to ping your server\'s endpoint:\n         `POST /api/scheduler/morning-routine` every day at `10:00 AM`."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 31318019
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
